      "content": "Vulnerable social pressure points are often found where routine meets high stakes, like during commuter rush hours or before major local events. Moments of enforced waiting, bureaucratic friction, or acute, low-level uncertainty are highly susceptible to emotional tipping points. Simple, non-invasive acts of shared acknowledgement or humor during these moments can act as friction reducers. Identifying these predictable points of friction in the community could help you be prepared to introduce a calming counter-signal when needed.",
